  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic empowerment</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mekong Plastic Innovation Hub program provided entrepreneurs with access to tailored business development services through a two stage program: the Incubator (for early-stage innovators) and Accelerator+ (for more advanced start-ups), concluding with a Demo Day where selected teams pitched their ventures to potential investors. The program is committed to fostering inclusive participation regardless of gender. In 2024, 19 women entrepreneurs &#x2013; either as team leads or key team members &#x2013; received support through expert-led training, mentorship, one-on-one coaching, technical assistance, and financial support to grow and refine their businesses. This included the standout team, Nopa Design from Vietnam which achieved significant growth during the program and successfully secured a grant from another project (Breaking the Plastic Habit in Asia Project) to advance their business. Women entrepreneurs made up 50 per cent of the teams advancing to Demo Day.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic empowerment</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mekong Plastics Innovation Alliance (MPIA) is a 3-year an investment that brings together entrepreneurs with scientific expertise to scale-up solutions to reduce plastic pollution in Mekong riverways. Fifty-two women from Thailand and Cambodia have been upskilled through capacity building to develop and refine their products, integrate sustainability and gender equality principles into their business models, pitch their solutions to investors, and engage in local and international network building and exchange.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
